["<task-notification>\n<task-id>ae235f8fed33e5578</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_018jKC3FQTxzvikpHKi2X6pE</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-youxun-project-game-agent-roguelite/7cf6507c-b688-43d0-9e91-b78620dd6a1f/tasks/ae235f8fed33e5578.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Feature: professional logging system\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>The logging system is built and committed on `feature/logging`. The headless bot run shows the error path working: a per-frame exception gets one full entry with game state and recent events, then only \"repeated N times\" summaries, a watchdog warning, and a top-repeated line in the footer. EditMode tests: 391/391 pass (335 existing + 56 new). Existing console lines are unchanged.\n\n## Research\nNotes are in `docs/research/logging.md`; every claim is marked as backed by a source or as my inference.\n\n| Idea | Decision | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| Listen to `Application.logMessageReceivedThreaded` | Adopt | Captures every existing `Debug.Log(\"[tag] …\")`, engine errors and `Update`/coroutine exceptions without changing console text. |\n| Replace `Debug.unityLogger.logHandler` | Skip | It would change the console stream the bot scripts grep. |\n| Unity Logging package (`com.unity.logging`) | Skip | Unity says it is for servers/Burst and \"not a complete replacement\" for `Debug.Log`. |\n| Sentry SDK | Skip | Needs a server. I copied its ideas: 100 breadcrumbs, context on errors, screenshot attachment. |\n| Sentry-style debounce (drop repeats) | Adapted | We count and summarise repeats instead, because the rate is the diagnosis. |\n| Async writer with a capped queue | Adopt, changed | Serilog and NLog drop the arriving entry when full; we drop the oldest least severe entry, so Debug spam can never push out an Error. |\n| Per-session rolling files with retention | Adopt | Scaled-down Serilog defaults: last 20 sessions, 200 MB total, 100 MB per session. |\n\nWhat I couldn't find: an official Unity statement that the threaded log event runs on the logging thread itself (the no-duplicates guard depends on this; I confirmed it in a run instead), an official Epic page on log backups, and published studio conventions for how long to keep player logs.\n\n## What was built\n- **Pure logic** (`unity/Assets/Scripts/Core/Logging/`):\n  - `Log.For(\"X\")` with `Trace…Fatal`, cheap `IsEnabled` checks, optional exception and properties.\n  - Levels from `AGENT_LOG_LEVEL`, e.g. `info,speech=trace`; default is Debug in the editor, Info in a build.\n  - Parsing of the leading `[tag]` into a category.\n  - Text and JSONL formats, the repeat counter, breadcrumbs, pluggable context providers, the capped queue, retention rules, and the background file writer.\n- **Runtime** (`unity/Assets/Scripts/Game/Features/Logging/`):\n  - Starts before the first scene loads.\n  - Session files: `session-*.log` + `.jsonl` + `latest.log`.\n  - Captures everything Unity logs, plus `AppDomain` unhandled and unobserved-task exceptions.\n  - Session header and footer; warns at startup if the previous session closed uncleanly.\n  - Detects a script reload during Play.\n  - A `[GameModule(0)]` that adds game state to every error (phase, room, runs, boss, player hp, enemy count, `ctx.Paused`/`Running`, timeScale, `Juice` base scale, settings, module list) and records breadcrumbs.\n  - Watches timeScale, frame spikes, and errors repeating every frame.\n  - F8 bug-report bundle with screenshot, plus a throttled automatic mini-report on each new error.\n  - `AGENT_LOG_SELFTEST=1`, kept as a documented debug tool.\n- **Docs:** `docs/specs/logging.md`, a logging section and env vars in `CLAUDE.md`, and an entry in the docs index.\n\n`ScreenshotTool` gained a `RenderToPng` method; `Capture` behaves exactly as before.\n\n## Evidence\nI ran three headless bot runs in my own scratch copy.\n\n**Run 1** (with the selftest) produced this session file:\n```\n2026-10-18 02:30:44.942 f=30 ERROR main [Exception] InvalidOperationException: selftest: thrown from Update every frame\n    ! LogSelfTest.Update () (at Assets/Scripts/Game/Features/Logging/LogSelfTest.cs:48)\n    context:  frame=30 timeScale=4 phase=Fight room=0 player=hp 100/100 enemies=2 ctx.Paused=False ctx.Running=True juice.BaseScale=4 …\n    breadcrumbs (9): [Phase] Hub -&gt; Fight … [SelfTest] selftest: handled error logged through the API\n2026-10-18 02:30:55.325 f=19312 ERROR main [Exception] repeated 119 more times in the last 10.4 s (total 120): …  everyFrame = True\n2026-10-18 02:30:55.325 f=19312 WARN  main [Watchdog] the same error is raised every frame (119 times in 119 frames) …\n… [Session] === SESSION END === clean=true reason=quit   count.error=122  suppressedRepeats=123  droppedEntries=0\n    topRepeated.1 = 120x ERROR [Exception] InvalidOperationException: … @ LogSelfTest.Update () (…:48)\n```\n- All 166 JSONL lines parse as valid JSON.\n- The error logged through the new API appears once in the console and once in the file, so nothing is logged twice.\n- 102 timeScale-change lines were recorded.\n- The auto report and the selftest report were both written (`context.json`, `breadcrumbs.txt`, `error.txt`, the log tail, `settings.json`, and a 499 KB `screenshot.png`).\n- The `[RUN]`, `[BOT]`, `[module]`, `[music]`, `[PLAN]`, `[PLAN-RULE]` and `[COMPANION]` console lines are unchanged.\n\n**Run 2** (after I deleted the first session's footer, with `AGENT_LOG_LEVEL=info`): it logged a Warn that the previous session did not shut down cleanly, with the file path, and wrote 0 Debug lines.\n\n**Run 3** (after the silent-catch cleanup): passed cleanly.\n\n**Fixes I made from reviewing run 1:**\n- The \"timeScale flapping\" warning fired 5 times during normal hit-stops, so I raised the threshold from 8 to 30 changes per second; run 2 had none.\n- I renamed my `[Run]` category so a case-insensitive grep for `[RUN]` cannot match it.\n- I removed a byte-order mark from the report files.\n\n**Found on the way:** every bot run, including other agents' runs from main, logs an `ArgumentOutOfRangeException` from Unity's own QuickSearch indexer (`SearchDatabase.GetDefaultSearchDatabase`) at startup. It now shows up in the session file; it is not caused by game code.\n\n## Swallowed catches\n14 catches did nothing at all; all now log, in their own commit, with behaviour unchanged:\n- `Core/AgentJson.cs:14` — JSON parse (Debug)\n- `Game/Agents/PiRpcChannel.cs:63` — JSON parse (Debug)\n- `Game/Agents/PiRpcChannel.cs:116`, `:117` — process kill/dispose (Debug)\n- `Game/Speech/SpeechSynth.cs:178` — JSON parse (Debug)\n- `Game/Speech/SpeechSynth.cs:204`, `:205`, `:206`, `:247`, `:255`, `:265` — process cleanup (Debug)\n- `Game/Speech/SpeechSynth.cs:210` — temp-file delete (Debug)\n- `Game/Speech/SpeechDirector.cs:50` — TTS temp-dir reset (Warn, since it affects TTS)\n- `Game/Speech/SpeechDirector.cs:347` — temp-dir cleanup (Debug)\n\n`Game/App/Modules/GameModules.cs:52` already handled a partial type-load failure; it now also logs a Warn.\n\n## Limits\n- **Script reload during Play is untested.** Restarting the logger after a reload can't be triggered headless; it needs a real editor session.\n- **Logging state is global.** `Log` is a deliberate global static, documented as the one exception to the no-singletons rule.\n- **Screenshots miss the HUD.** They don't include IMGUI (HUD, pause menu), same as `ScreenshotTool`.\n- **No remote upload.** Report folders are attached to bug reports by hand.\n- **A native crash leaves no footer.** The next startup's warning is the only signal, and up to about 1 s of Info/Debug lines may be lost; Errors are flushed to disk immediately.\n- **Secrets are only masked in the header.** Environment variables are masked by name; messages are not checked.\n- **`.meta` files are now committed** for the new folders, unlike `BossIntro`, which has none.\n\n## Commits (`git -C WT log --oneline main..HEAD`)\n```\n648a558 Docs: logging spec and CLAUDE.md conventions\n78e1aa0 Log the exceptions that were swallowed silently\n335c1d2 Runtime logging: session files, Unity log bridge, game context, F8 bug reports\n6777380 Core logging: levels, pipeline, dedupe, breadcrumbs, context, async file sink\n81b116e Research: how Unity, Sentry, Serilog/NLog/M.E.Logging and games do logging\n```\nThe worktree is clean.\n\nFiles are in /Users/youxun/project/game/agent-roguelite-worktrees/logging:\n- docs/research/logging.md\n- docs/specs/logging.md\n- unity/Assets/Scripts/Core/Logging/\n- unity/Assets/Scripts/Game/Features/Logging/\n\nEvidence is in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-youxun-project-game-agent-roguelite/7cf6507c-b688-43d0-9e91-b78620dd6a1f/scratchpad:\n- tests-logging.xml\n- logs-run1-backup/session-20261018-023044.log\n- logs-run1-backup/reports/\n- logs-test/session-20261018-071213.log\n- bot-logging.log</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>280827</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>24</tool_uses><duration_ms>317555</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"]
