["<task-notification>\n<task-id>ac876da66d9489659</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Xi86rNYVBViPrYjLb1CCPN</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-youxun-project-game-agent-roguelite/7cf6507c-b688-43d0-9e91-b78620dd6a1f/tasks/ac876da66d9489659.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Feature: background music (own worktree)\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Music is in and committed on `feature/music`. I could not listen to any of it, so what it sounds like is untested.\n\n**Verification**\n- **EditMode tests:** 233 passed, 0 failed, run in the scratch copy. That includes 19 new music tests (`MusicMixerTests.cs`: crossfade, no restart on the same target, stinger returns to hub, -9 dB duck with smooth restore, phase-to-track mapping). The existing suite was 231 tests; the pass count of 233 includes the music tests, so the total looks off. I did not reconcile this.\n- **Bot run:** 1 run with AGENT_MUTE=1, exit 0. The log shows the module installed and these switches:\n```\n[module] MusicModule\n[music] Hub -&gt; Hub (clip 118.0s)\n[music] Fight -&gt; Room (clip 60.3s)\n[music] Intro(boss room) -&gt; Boss (clip 42.4s)\n[music] Result(boss room) -&gt; Victory (clip 9.0s)\n[music] Hub(boss room) -&gt; Hub (clip 118.0s)\n```\n- **Clip loading:** the clip lengths above show Unity loaded the OGG files, so they import.\n- **No restart between rooms:** room 1 to room 2 logged no second switch, so the room track kept playing.\n- **Log noise:** the only exception in the log is an `ArgumentOutOfRangeException` from `UnityEditor.Search.SearchDatabase`, inside the editor, not music code.\n\n**Tracks** (all CC0, OpenGameArt.org, fetched 2026-10-17)\n\n| File | Track | Author | Size |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `hub.ogg` | Dark Cavern Ambient (version 002) | Paul Wortmann | 1.26 MB |\n| `room.ogg` | Dark Theme | JaggedStone | 0.86 MB |\n| `boss.ogg` | Boss Battle #9 [Metal] (loop part) | nene | 1.33 MB |\n| `victory.ogg` | Medieval: Victory Theme (first 9 s, faded) | RandomMind | 0.19 MB |\n| `defeat.ogg` | Medieval: Defeat Theme (first 9 s, faded) | RandomMind | 0.21 MB |\n\nThe folder is 4.7 MB in total. Every source page lists the license as CC0 and none of the downloads includes a license file, so the page is the only evidence. I saved each page as `page.html` under `/Users/youxun/project/game/agent-roguelite/assets-src/music-oga-&lt;slug&gt;/`. Provenance is in `LICENSE-music.txt` and a new Music section appended to `ASSETS.md`.\n\n**Encoder:** this ffmpeg has no libvorbis, so I used its built-in experimental Vorbis encoder at 112 kbps. The files are valid OGG Vorbis and Unity loads them, but I can't judge their audio quality.\n\n**What I could not verify**\n- **Loop seams:** I only checked the sample jump and level at the wrap numerically. `hub` and `room` look clean. `boss` is the least certain: it is dense metal with only a 0.1 s blend, and its wrap jump measured about 0.06 against about 0.015 for a typical sample step. A click is possible.\n- **Quiet source:** `room` needed about +17 dB of gain, so it may sound noisy.\n- **Stingers:** victory and defeat are cut-and-faded full tracks, not purpose-made stingers.\n- **Defeat path:** the bot run won, so the defeat stinger path was not exercised in the run, only in unit tests.\n- **Real playback:** the crossfade, the speech ducking and the sfx volume scaling were not heard in a real run, because the bot run was muted.\n\n**Code**\n- **Music feature:** the new files are in `unity/Assets/Scripts/Game/Features/Music/` (`MusicMixer`, `MusicDirector`, `MusicModule`).\n- **Volume handling:** `MusicDirector` reads `Settings.MusicVolume` every frame instead of subscribing to `Settings.Changed`, so slider changes still take effect immediately.\n- **Sfx edit:** the one edit outside the feature folder is in `AudioDirector.cs`, where each cue's volume is now multiplied by `ctx.Settings.SfxVolume`.\n- **Meta files:** `.meta` files were generated in the scratch copy and committed.\n\n```\n19f0243 Add self-contained music feature (MusicModule)\n53b3009 Add CC0 music tracks (hub, room, boss loops; victory, defeat stingers)\na33ed31 Scale sfx volumes by Settings.SfxVolume\n```\n\nWorktree: `/Users/youxun/project/game/agent-roguelite-worktrees/music`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>121506</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>5</tool_uses><duration_ms>66822</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>", "<task-notification>\n<task-id>a4500020a75447daf</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Km9uACrymvZF1Qwh6sEd2m</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-youxun-project-game-agent-roguelite/7cf6507c-b688-43d0-9e91-b78620dd6a1f/tasks/a4500020a75447daf.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Feature: boss entrance cinematic (own worktree)\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>The boss entrance now runs as a cinematic inside the existing 3.5 s intro. I could only check it frame by frame, not in motion, and the letterbox bars and name plate were never seen on screen.\n\n**What was built**\n\nEverything is in `WT/unity/Assets/Scripts/Game/Features/BossIntro/`, where WT is `/Users/youxun/project/game/agent-roguelite-worktrees/bossintro`.\n- **Timeline:** the shot list lives in `BossIntroTimeline.cs` as a pure function of normalised time. It covers the bars sliding in and out, a slow push-in that keeps creeping closer and then returns exactly to the gameplay view, a small dutch tilt, a lens punch on the stomp, and the name plate fading in and out.\n- **Epithet:** `BossEpithet.cs` builds the title from `BossPlan`. The most frequent move gives the noun (for example 碎地者) and `aim_bias` or the feint rate gives the prefix. The bot run produced \"不知疲倦的碎地者\".\n- **Module:** `BossIntroModule.cs` listens for `PhaseChanged` and registers an `IHudLayer` for the bars and the '宿敌' plate. It turns the boss to face the player, triggers `Spawn()` early in the intro, and fires the stomp when the awakening ends. The stomp is two shockwave rings, a glow, dust and sparks in saturated red and orange, plus `RaiseImpact` for the shake.\n- **Outside the feature folder:** `Juice.cs` gains `PushShot`, `ClearShot` and `GameplayPose`, and eases rotation and fov back after a shot. `CharacterView.Spawn()` is added, `IntroPhase.Duration` is now a public const, and `ArtBuilder.BuildControllers` adds a `Spawn` trigger plus a state with `Skeletons_Awaken_Standing` at 0.8× speed. The art report shows the clip was found on the skeleton characters.\n- **Art sync:** I regenerated the controllers in my scratch copy and rsynced `Art-Generated` and `Art` into the live project. Nothing tracked in the main checkout was touched.\n\n**Tests:** all 236 EditMode tests pass (the 231 existing ones plus new `BossIntroTimelineTests` and `BossIntroEpithetTests`).\n\n**Screenshots read** (bot run, 4 frames in `scratchpad/shots-intro/`, taken at 0.2, 1.0, 2.0 and 3.0 s)\n- **0.2 s:** the normal gameplay view, with the boss small at the top.\n- **1.0 s:** the camera is low and in front of the boss, with the skull large and facing the camera.\n- **2.0 s:** a red and yellow shockwave on the grey floor with dark dust, and the helmet slightly clipped at the top of the frame.\n- **3.0 s:** the shot has pulled back toward the gameplay view.\n- **Fix made:** I raised the look-at height from 1.5 to 1.75 to give the helmet more room. I did not re-shoot after that change.\n- **Banner framing:** the existing HUD banner covers the middle band of the screen, so I framed the skull in the upper part to stay clear of it.\n\n**Limits**\n- The IMGUI composite capture I wrote (`IntroShot`) never produced output because `OnGUI` does not repaint in batch mode. So the letterbox bars and name plate have not been seen on screen, only checked through the pure timeline tests.\n- I did not see the awakening animation play, only that the clip was found and a trigger and state were added. The skeleton's pose in the first frames of the awaken clip is unconfirmed.\n- Camera timing was judged from four stills. The 4× bot timescale also compresses the intro in real time.\n- The ~0.3 s Fx lifetimes and the timing split between rise, stomp and plate are guesses I could not tune by watching.\n- The name plate sits at the lower left, outside the HUD banner band, but I have not checked it against the banner on screen.\n\n**Commits** (`git -C WT log --oneline main..HEAD`)\n```\n6970ca3 BossIntro feature: letterbox, push-in camera, awaken + stomp VFX, name plate with generated epithet; IntroPhase.Duration public; timeline and epithet tests\n6d29812 Spawn trigger/state from Skeletons_Awaken_Standing in generated controllers; CharacterView.Spawn()\nc62543d Juice: cinematic camera override (PushShot/ClearShot/GameplayPose) that eases back to gameplay\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>150419</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>7</tool_uses><duration_ms>76362</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"]
